<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kenny Anthony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1951</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Kenny D. Anthony</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kenny Anthony is a Saint Lucian lawyer and politician who led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-lucia-labour-party">Saint Lucia Labour Party</a> and served as Prime Minister of Saint Lucia from 1997 to 2006 and again from 2011 to 2016. His first government came to power as the island's banana industry collapsed with the loss of preferential access to European markets, and it encouraged the shift of the economy towards tourism and services.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kenny-anthony.jpg" alt="Kenny Anthony" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: National Police of Colombia · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VI_Cumbre_de_las_Am%C3%A9ricas_(7077114569)_(cropped)_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
